/**
@mainpage Cortex Coroutine Library

@section intro Introduction
Cortex is a C++ stackful coroutine library with WebAssembly (Emscripten) support.
It provides cooperative multitasking with explicit suspend/resume semantics and
works across native and WASM builds through a unified API.

@section highlights Highlights
- Stackful coroutines with a simple @c Resume / @c Suspend model
- Unified API for native (Boost.Context) and WASM (Emscripten fibers)
- @b tiny_fiber module for single-thread cooperative multitasking (native + WASM)
- @b fiber module for multithreaded cooperative multitasking (native only)
- Custom memory resource support for stack allocation
- Designed for deterministic, cooperative control flow

@section quickstart Quick Start
@code
#include <cortex/coroutine.hpp>

auto co = cortex::Coroutine::Make([](cortex::CoroutineSuspendContext& ctx) {
    // Do work...
    ctx.Suspend(); // Yield back to caller
    // Resume here...
});

co.Resume();
co.Resume();
@endcode

@section tinyfiber tiny_fiber Module
Higher-level cooperative multitasking built on Coroutine:
@code
#include <cortex/tiny_fiber/tiny_fiber.hpp>
namespace tf = cortex::tiny_fiber;

tf::Scheduler::Run([] {
    auto future = tf::Spawn([] {
        tf::Yield();  // Cooperative yield
        return 42;
    });
    
    tf::Yield();
    int result = future.Get();  // Wait and get result
});
@endcode

For WASM integration with JS event loop:
@code
auto scheduler = tf::Scheduler::Create([]{
    // Spawn fibers, use Mutex, ConditionVariable, etc.
});

// Called from JS via setInterval
while (!scheduler.IsDone()) {
    scheduler.Step();  // Run one fiber until yield
}
@endcode

@section fiber fiber Module (Native Only)
Multithreaded cooperative multitasking with worker threads and work stealing:
@code
#include <cortex/fiber/fiber.hpp>
namespace ff = cortex::fiber;

ff::Scheduler::Run([] {
    auto future = ff::Spawn([] {
        ff::Yield();
        return 42;
    });

    int result = future.Get();
});
@endcode

@note @b cortex::fiber is not available on WebAssembly. Use @b cortex::tiny_fiber in WASM builds.

@section generator Generator Example
@code
#include <cortex/generator.hpp>

auto gen = cortex::Generator<int>::Make([](auto& yield) {
    yield(1);
    yield(2);
    yield(3);
});

while (gen.Next()) {
    int value = gen.DetachValue();
    // use value
}
@endcode

@section structure API Overview
- @ref cortex::Coroutine "Coroutine": low-level stackful coroutine
- @ref cortex::BaseCoroutine "BaseCoroutine": OO wrapper for coroutines
- @ref cortex::Generator "Generator": yield values across resumes
- @ref cortex::tiny_fiber "tiny_fiber": single-thread cooperative fibers (native + WASM)
- @ref cortex::fiber "fiber": multithreaded cooperative fibers (native only)

@section resources Resources
- Live demos: https://GhevondW.github.io/cortex/
- API docs: https://GhevondW.github.io/cortex/docs/
*/
